<div class="note"><b class="h">Local claim risks</b><ul class="chips" style="margin:10px 0 0"><li>Ice storms</li><li>Wildfire smoke</li><li>Windstorms</li><li>Tornado (rare)</li><li>Frozen pipes</li></ul></div>

<h2>Salem at a glance</h2>
<p>Salem is Oregon’s capital and the seat of Marion County; West Salem lies across the Willamette River in Polk County. Neighborhoods range from historic homes near the Capitol and in the Grant and Court-Chemeketa areas to mid-century ranch houses in South Salem and newer subdivisions on the edges of town. The state’s insurance regulator, the Division of Financial Regulation, is based here.</p>
<h2>Storms and fires that shaped Salem claims</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>The February 2021 ice storm</strong> was one of the worst in the city’s memory, with trees down across neighborhoods and many homes without power for days.</li>
<li><strong>The 2020 Labor Day fires</strong>, especially Beachie Creek and Lionshead, burned through the Santiam Canyon east of Salem, destroying homes in Detroit, Gates and Mill City and blanketing the city in smoke.</li>
<li><strong>The December 2010 Aumsville tornado</strong>, an EF2, struck a small town just southeast of Salem.</li>
<li><strong>Winter windstorms</strong> bring down limbs and damage roofs every season.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Claims we see in Salem</h2>
<p>Tree impacts on older homes, ice-related pipe bursts, smoke infiltration in homes that survived nearby fires, and roof claims after windstorms. Older homes with plaster walls and original finishes need careful pricing.</p>

<h2>Neighborhoods we cover</h2>
<p>We inspect homes and buildings throughout Salem, including West Salem, South Salem, Grant, Northeast Neighbors, Sunnyslope, Morningside and Highland, and the surrounding parts of Marion County.</p>
<h2>Services available in Salem</h2>
<p>Every Oregon Insurance Appraiser service is available to property owners in Salem, including:</p>
<ul><li><a href="/property-appraisals/appraisal-clause-help/">Appraisal Clause Representation</a></li><li><a href="/property-appraisals/home-insurance-appraisal/">Homeowner Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/property-appraisals/commercial-hoa-appraisal/">Commercial &amp; HOA Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/property-appraisals/roof-hail-appraisal/">Roof &amp; Hail Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/property-appraisals/windstorm-tornado-appraisal/">Windstorm &amp; Tornado Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/property-appraisals/ice-storm-snow-appraisal/">Ice Storm &amp; Snow Load Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/property-appraisals/water-damage-appraisal/">Water Damage Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/property-appraisals/house-fire-smoke-appraisal/">Fire &amp; Smoke Damage Appraisal</a></li></ul>
<h2>Questions from Salem property owners</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Do you handle Santiam Canyon wildfire claims?</summary><div class="a"><p>Yes. We work with property owners in the canyon and around Salem on rebuild, contents and smoke claims.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can I file a complaint with the state about my claim?</summary><div class="a"><p>Yes. The Oregon Division of Financial Regulation accepts consumer complaints. That process is separate from appraisal, and you can use both.</p></div></details><details><summary>Do you cover Polk County too?</summary><div class="a"><p>Yes, including West Salem, Dallas, Monmouth and Independence.</p></div></details></div>
